estion/id #uuid "a5ddbd9f-8150-5833-819a-e65c26b2e497" :question/math-academy-id "q-115205" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2{e}^{x-2}+1<3.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{x-2}+1 & <3 \\\\ 2{e}^{x-2} & <2 \\\\ {e}^{x-2} & <1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x-2}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\ x-2 & <0 \\\\ x & <2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115205/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "04309d45-2991-5d4b-9dc9-b75422610ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115205"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277847/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer/id #uuid "11247a3f-26f3-5730-b560-14e9bc3fec26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277847/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "16f353a0-630f-5937-ba75-6adb97e42f0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277847/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-277847/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277847/field-2/2362d71a61a1ac2265d5d6c766e16f1683e792d375c9bdee9fd7fcbd8229514f" :answer/id #uuid "3d1417a4-eea8-575c-84d4-7a320c1b45c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\ln(12)}{\\ln(9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277847/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "351a3c4f-018c-57d0-8db2-1034d851cdd5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277847/field-2/2362d71a61a1ac2265d5d6c766e16f1683e792d375c9bdee9fd7fcbd8229514f" :answer-field/choices ["q-277847/field-2/2362d71a61a1ac2265d5d6c766e16f1683e792d375c9bdee9fd7fcbd8229514f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277847" :question/id #uuid "b74d80da-84b6-5b4d-af66-de07a7526db7" :question/math-academy-id "q-277847" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $8\\cdot {9}^{x}\\ge \\frac{2}{3}.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\cdot {9}^{x} & \\ge \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ {9}^{x} & \\ge \\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the logarithm to base $9$ of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{9}⁡({9}^{x}) & \\ge {log}_{9}⁡(\\frac{1}{12}) \\\\ {log}_{9}⁡({9}^{x}) & \\ge {log}_{9}⁡({12}^{-1}) \\\\ x & \\ge -{log}_{9}⁡(12).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-277847/field-1" "q-277847/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "04309d45-2991-5d4b-9dc9-b75422610ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277846/field-1/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer/id #uuid "fb1fa160-55f8-5a70-91a9-35c92680ac06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277846/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "78682677-fcab-5274-af12-4b1dcd9d5281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277846/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7e11152-bd30-5485-9804-f461f5a0895e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277846/field-1/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-277846/field-1/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" "q-277846/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277846/field-2/87a7e0f1b3f6cd8410e33bfa11ceb5c40a774499792ca9474eda3bc5051a0ff1" :answer/id #uuid "11f1f561-10ad-59a2-b058-10363ae0d32c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln(14)}{\\ln(4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277846/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b1ad023-ebec-5f19-95cc-47e1b6b7e605" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277846/field-2/87a7e0f1b3f6cd8410e33bfa11ceb5c40a774499792ca9474eda3bc5051a0ff1" :answer-field/choices ["q-277846/field-2/87a7e0f1b3f6cd8410e33bfa11ceb5c40a774499792ca9474eda3bc5051a0ff1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277846" :question/id #uuid "f8711faf-ad47-5c1d-b8a5-bf5e50a40321" :question/math-academy-id "q-277846" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{x}>7.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{x} & >7 \\\\ {4}^{x} & >14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the logarithm to base $4$ of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{x}) & >{log}_{4}⁡(14) \\\\ x & >{log}_{4}⁡(14).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-277846/field-1" "q-277846/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "04309d45-2991-5d4b-9dc9-b75422610ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277853/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "58084965-2217-5fb7-a5a8-ece0b61b6082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277853/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a8692b-8a83-5a1d-950f-d8d7dae08f9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277853/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-277853/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277853/field-2/8252a9d966a9c43038e2fbeaf2832b46b26d9878462ae8d62b98625fd3214ab8" :answer/id #uuid "67391286-5a5f-51c4-a511-707250724944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{\\ln(3)}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277853/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8bf2fbc-0be1-5b22-938b-6ca26cf79bac" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277853/field-2/8252a9d966a9c43038e2fbeaf2832b46b26d9878462ae8d62b98625fd3214ab8" :answer-field/choices ["q-277853/field-2/8252a9d966a9c43038e2fbeaf2832b46b26d9878462ae8d62b98625fd3214ab8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277853" :question/id #uuid "2083d32e-7721-5866-8074-0c239f215fa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-277853" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{3{e}^{2-3x}}{\\sqrt{3}}<-2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{3{e}^{2-3x}}{\\sqrt{3}} & <-2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\frac{3{e}^{2-3x}}{\\sqrt{3}} & <-3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3{e}^{2-3x} & <-3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3{e}^{2-3x} & <-9 \\\\ {e}^{2-3x} & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2-3x}) & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ 2-3x & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ -3x & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2 \\\\ 3x & <2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ x & <\\frac{1}{3}(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-277853/field-1" "q-277853/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "04309d45-2991-5d4b-9dc9-b75422610ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277844/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer/id #uuid "28173a38-6dc9-5fd2-a61c-f52b4f6e70e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277844/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8db2f32b-274d-5e59-a578-1054bbe672fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277844/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-277844/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277844/field-2/4ccc1caa91bb2c598a80e96d7e6411a86223317763545e223ece1cc0480ea3ae" :answer/id #uuid "2459edc8-1840-550d-919b-e265dd3af5bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln(24)}{2\\ln(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277844/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa7f84d-4a73-563e-b878-79f01f074242" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277844/field-2/4ccc1caa91bb2c598a80e96d7e6411a86223317763545e223ece1cc0480ea3ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-277844/field-2/4ccc1caa91bb2c598a80e96d7e6411a86223317763545e223ece1cc0480ea3ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277844" :question/id #uuid "dd62bfd9-6b42-572a-8c38-43a6755aee95" :question/math-academy-id "q-277844" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {3}^{2x-1}\\ge 2.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {3}^{2x-1} & \\ge 2 \\\\ {3}^{2x-1} & \\ge 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the logarithm to base $3$ of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{2x-1}) & \\ge {log}_{3}⁡(8) \\\\ 2x-1 & \\ge {log}_{3}⁡(8) \\\\ 2x & \\ge {log}_{3}⁡(8)+1 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{1}{2}({log}_{3}⁡(8)+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-277844/field-1" "q-277844/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "04309d45-2991-5d4b-9dc9-b75422610ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277844"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212/selection/9bc46ebf51c61de67f4eafaeaecc67143967bcc97c56f8cfb28c32ad70bd9871" :answer/id #uuid "5988bfda-7332-516f-8edd-453ba7812201" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212/selection/6fe489b9bc7437788c0449de0a1baf73a14f55159a6018218cddfa8234c7df66" :answer/id #uuid "b8deb015-650a-5e4b-82bf-eca48b4c62e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212/selection/2daa2722bb61fda366d9cb944a0aed7cc0bcb5c7f552f046f5cda017ab73b245" :answer/id #uuid "d46004f7-34ec-5bd0-b351-1705c4d16eac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212/selection/225f33685a36069a22c9b1b25215bcf33c5ee17186fdf325218e21ce7c9c5955" :answer/id #uuid "3101d6b6-76c6-5bfd-9ca7-5e4ce12c4c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212/selection/05700156fb859afba57439170fac4c826b9197e3ae828808ee8f6901caaacdd1" :answer/id #uuid "31524f6f-9455-5698-839b-7c8011f5f2fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e11fd5a1-6666-52f1-95ec-ed1f9256af9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115212/selection/2daa2722bb61fda366d9cb944a0aed7cc0bcb5c7f552f046f5cda017ab73b245" :answer-field/choices ["q-115212/selection/9bc46ebf51c61de67f4eafaeaecc67143967bcc97c56f8cfb28c32ad70bd9871" "q-115212/selection/6fe489b9bc7437788c0449de0a1baf73a14f55159a6018218cddfa8234c7df66" "q-115212/selection/2daa2722bb61fda366d9cb944a0aed7cc0bcb5c7f552f046f5cda017ab73b245" "q-115212/selection/225f33685a36069a22c9b1b25215bcf33c5ee17186fdf325218e21ce7c9c5955" "q-115212/selection/05700156fb859afba57439170fac4c826b9197e3ae828808ee8f6901caaacdd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115212" :question/id #uuid "f78e66ee-bef1-5f44-a0f0-8d3c8b5e36fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-115212" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2{(0.7)}^{x+9}\\ge 4.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(0.7)}^{x+9} & \\ge 4 \\\\ {(0.7)}^{x+9} & \\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[(0.7)^{x+9}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ (x+9)\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7 & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+9 & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7} \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05f94d64-fdf7-55d8-80fb-3988a47ed2d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833/selection/2c262074a40c5b137c3f1c93eb2e7ecab8e681ea2cbd5f3b920568bf1c6c2daa" :answer/id #uuid "7941a20d-a88d-520e-bc10-20960fa2afbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833/selection/0c137f2e70140928d190ea83b14333d104d81ec7ce62f5fdc334ad58111cc142" :answer/id #uuid "98c6be13-ee07-569e-b47a-a3b109110d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833/selection/059086341052aabfcf8969fdcc5b549a7a29606cb03d833aee8ec5a1cbbad4df" :answer/id #uuid "661dcbf8-3a68-5651-bff8-a48afc11bad2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833/selection/cb76b8c84601fc5337382f92571ddf58500fa8680cf77ea1bde94c9df97db361" :answer/id #uuid "dfbe2f79-a385-5aff-a677-4ae13f499f9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833/selection/0c1c15f213324767e73d17339dcefa2a46791353fc94266c4580d7e36b987e10" :answer/id #uuid "0feb2b7c-3f51-55cb-ac1a-97475cc2519b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8cd88b8-3264-561f-b984-78b8dbc1ea35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87833/selection/0c1c15f213324767e73d17339dcefa2a46791353fc94266c4580d7e36b987e10" :answer-field/choices ["q-87833/selection/2c262074a40c5b137c3f1c93eb2e7ecab8e681ea2cbd5f3b920568bf1c6c2daa" "q-87833/selection/0c137f2e70140928d190ea83b14333d104d81ec7ce62f5fdc334ad58111cc142" "q-87833/selection/059086341052aabfcf8969fdcc5b549a7a29606cb03d833aee8ec5a1cbbad4df" "q-87833/selection/cb76b8c84601fc5337382f92571ddf58500fa8680cf77ea1bde94c9df97db361" "q-87833/selection/0c1c15f213324767e73d17339dcefa2a46791353fc94266c4580d7e36b987e10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87833" :question/id #uuid "ead7b70a-ed06-52b4-b721-a1de1a689310" :question/math-academy-id "q-87833" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${(0.84)}^{x+5}-20>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(0.84)}^{x+5}-20 & >0 \\\\ {(0.84)}^{x+5} & >20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[(0.84)^{x+5}] & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20) \\\\ (x+5)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84) & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & <\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)} \\\\ x & <\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(20)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.84)}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87833/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05f94d64-fdf7-55d8-80fb-3988a47ed2d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308/selection/0dbfc379af15dab6a363c7b108ced19c5d954f117b593426e5aee9a54686f761" :answer/id #uuid "bd8e4cac-b7be-57e1-9847-86677d582263" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2e)}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308/selection/4ca377475f8ca44f12c2ce13331ca458cac718d855eb6018d5e8aecf713f82df" :answer/id #uuid "068e84d9-6429-5ecc-9038-e51b9a1cc340" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308/selection/2405f8f56645144beb8f78e6e5df2dbbf016e1ed0cdf57239717ad15661c136d" :answer/id #uuid "d3e983e0-872c-542b-b9fe-144d34374c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308/selection/d509c6d9648fd81b12611ed39e0c62bd3844a82efc93a002a111b7284de3c613" :answer/id #uuid "561c520d-a76c-579a-b020-79b30a676e0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308/selection/2337f8e5415ae913d3b272dd8672b2490d33c92521ae0362b4d572f211782a53" :answer/id #uuid "189672dd-70cb-541b-b857-64ffc4c2edb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebcf297-43e8-5786-9584-413e92833c2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365308/selection/2405f8f56645144beb8f78e6e5df2dbbf016e1ed0cdf57239717ad15661c136d" :answer-field/choices ["q-365308/selection/0dbfc379af15dab6a363c7b108ced19c5d954f117b593426e5aee9a54686f761" "q-365308/selection/4ca377475f8ca44f12c2ce13331ca458cac718d855eb6018d5e8aecf713f82df" "q-365308/selection/2405f8f56645144beb8f78e6e5df2dbbf016e1ed0cdf57239717ad15661c136d" "q-365308/selection/d509c6d9648fd81b12611ed39e0c62bd3844a82efc93a002a111b7284de3c613" "q-365308/selection/2337f8e5415ae913d3b272dd8672b2490d33c92521ae0362b4d572f211782a53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365308" :question/id #uuid "2927fe24-07db-5e34-9585-ee2e3af94b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-365308" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{3}{4}{(0.54)}^{x+3}-2e\\ge e.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{(0.54)}^{x+3}-2e & \\ge e \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}{(0.54)}^{x+3} & \\ge 3e \\\\ {(0.54)}^{x+3} & \\ge 4e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[(0.54)^{x+3}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e) \\\\ (x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54) & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)} \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4e)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.54)}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-365308/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05f94d64-fdf7-55d8-80fb-3988a47ed2d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828/selection/fb57eed147e12a90d1234d5d7acf2c8e6bd2d995afd3285a6228efbb48fce1bd" :answer/id #uuid "e70c3a62-ead6-5533-bec8-ab8aaba6337b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828/selection/979c935065fa32772ac80712e9ab75663e606443d74ba6151a5c8d4b5dc8d2f6" :answer/id #uuid "aa234ef4-ee3c-57db-82f5-c1d69e769d21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828/selection/577d8433b3b8e375f5c7a837e1abde2bbcb34b42cda5fa097eef7e5bc949cc2a" :answer/id #uuid "f2116fb8-7bb1-5de7-b7ae-dedf7e9021c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828/selection/7f2932011d97fdb686f051de6f68788b2773fb55f5cbb81d0a37206d4ffddd27" :answer/id #uuid "5bce91c7-2378-5550-b238-6fda7740fe7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828/selection/424ac766f522d68caba8b1cecb4937c606ee480f05b36fa7c5ccc646101e27c7" :answer/id #uuid "5a7d1d1a-ed8a-5886-bde3-d2c482abe3d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be109be0-7d81-59f9-8107-12d4523a5e57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87828/selection/424ac766f522d68caba8b1cecb4937c606ee480f05b36fa7c5ccc646101e27c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-87828/selection/fb57eed147e12a90d1234d5d7acf2c8e6bd2d995afd3285a6228efbb48fce1bd" "q-87828/selection/979c935065fa32772ac80712e9ab75663e606443d74ba6151a5c8d4b5dc8d2f6" "q-87828/selection/577d8433b3b8e375f5c7a837e1abde2bbcb34b42cda5fa097eef7e5bc949cc2a" "q-87828/selection/7f2932011d97fdb686f051de6f68788b2773fb55f5cbb81d0a37206d4ffddd27" "q-87828/selection/424ac766f522d68caba8b1cecb4937c606ee480f05b36fa7c5ccc646101e27c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87828" :question/id #uuid "078bdf1c-b6d1-5ab4-9023-b94588024657" :question/math-academy-id "q-87828" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $5\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{x}<25.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{x} & <25 \\\\ {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{x} & <5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{x}] & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{9}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & >\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05f94d64-fdf7-55d8-80fb-3988a47ed2d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222/selection/e2006e2529390cf92136b28780c57974f077c1b63768f24fc98b31fad816e579" :answer/id #uuid "4bae2ce8-d17c-5660-8dd4-c21070826cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222/selection/ad2f8e8c0ea9ee9695c15030eb3e1b745087a9b672ab8f7c8a2af2fa6ec5202c" :answer/id #uuid "c1f78af6-c7ed-5d65-a74b-7108b8a9aa16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222/selection/fd975b387798d68b47232e359ec9a23ec1ccc2414f425260423c490f8397461a" :answer/id #uuid "b1352605-6ad5-5065-bec5-692305ff4b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer/id #uuid "41e303d1-33ee-53bf-90d9-c30bb87fe7d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222/selection/de8ab916eeab3df2354c51c7ee5b34385aa2a1675f8435f71d9e18ce0ed20afc" :answer/id #uuid "b0c2e384-c1a0-5f8b-9458-7ddb2be0f3fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb532446-b49d-5fdb-9992-a86be9d0391b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115222/selection/fd975b387798d68b47232e359ec9a23ec1ccc2414f425260423c490f8397461a" :answer-field/choices ["q-115222/selection/e2006e2529390cf92136b28780c57974f077c1b63768f24fc98b31fad816e579" "q-115222/selection/ad2f8e8c0ea9ee9695c15030eb3e1b745087a9b672ab8f7c8a2af2fa6ec5202c" "q-115222/selection/fd975b387798d68b47232e359ec9a23ec1ccc2414f425260423c490f8397461a" "q-115222/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" "q-115222/selection/de8ab916eeab3df2354c51c7ee5b34385aa2a1675f8435f71d9e18ce0ed20afc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115222" :question/id #uuid "53c92145-52c7-5881-9ab5-7c588ac0f4ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-115222" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}+1\\ge 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}+1 & \\ge 2 \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6} & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\ (x+6)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+6)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+6)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6) & \\le \\frac{0}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ x+6 & \\le 0 \\\\ x & \\le -6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115222/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05f94d64-fdf7-55d8-80fb-3988a47ed2d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115230/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" :answer/id #uuid "53e86893-596b-51f4-a5e4-08f245fe9437" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115230/selection/1a682cf8896506668f7e51963db4bd9e20e26bf0c13c16dce6d12eea53ea6d90" :answer/id #uuid "c14fb307-133d-52b2-b4bc-1d9